---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import '../styles/global.css';

// Mention Microsoft Clarity in the policy only when the BaseLayout
// is actually loading it (gated by the same env var).
const clarityEnabled = !!import.meta.env.PUBLIC_CLARITY_PROJECT_ID;
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy | A-Worthy Singapore Tuition" description="A-Worthy's privacy policy. How we collect, use, and protect your personal data in accordance with Singapore's Personal Data Protection Act (PDPA).">
  <Header slot="header" />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container policy-content">
      <span class="eyebrow">Privacy Policy</span>
      <h1 class="policy-title squiggle">Privacy Policy&nbsp;&mdash; <span class="nowrap">A-Worthy</span> Pte Ltd</h1>
      <p class="policy-updated">Last updated: September 2026</p>

      <p>A-Worthy Pte Ltd (&ldquo;A-Worthy&rdquo;, &ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo;, or &ldquo;our&rdquo;) operates the website at <a href="https://a-worthy.com">a-worthy.com</a>. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and protect your personal data in accordance with Singapore&rsquo;s <strong>Personal Data Protection Act 2012 (PDPA)</strong>.</p>

      <p>By using our website or submitting your information through our forms, you consent to the practices described in this policy.</p>

      <h2>1. Data we collect</h2>
      <p>We collect personal data only when you actively provide it to us. This includes:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Contact and enquiry forms</strong> &mdash; your name, email address, phone number, and any details you include in your message (for example, your child&rsquo;s level and the subject you&rsquo;re interested in). Each enquiry also carries the page it was sent from and how you reached our website (see &ldquo;Enquiry source&rdquo; in Section 2).</li>
        <li><strong>Resource and guide requests</strong> &mdash; your email address, and any other details the form asks for, when you request a free resource or subject guide.</li>
        <li><strong>WhatsApp</strong> &mdash; if you contact us via WhatsApp, your phone number and message content are processed through WhatsApp LLC under its own privacy policy. A message started from a button on our website includes a short reference, such as <code>[ref: PRICING]</code>, naming the page you wrote from and, where there is one, the advertising source.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not collect payment card data. All payment processing, if applicable, is handled by third-party providers under their own privacy policies.</p>
      <p>We do not knowingly collect personal data from children under 13 without verifiable parental consent.</p>

      <h2>2. Cookies and analytics</h2>
      <p>Our website uses the following cookies, browser storage and scripts:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Essential cookies</strong> &mdash; required for the site to function correctly (for example, your theme preference stored in <code>localStorage</code>).</li>
        <li><strong>Service worker cache</strong> &mdash; a service worker caches static assets for faster load times and offline access. No personal data is stored in this cache.</li>
        <li><strong>Plausible Analytics</strong> &mdash; we use Plausible, a privacy-friendly, GDPR-compliant analytics tool that does not use cookies and does not collect personally identifiable information. Aggregate traffic data (page views, referrers, country) is recorded anonymously. We also count clicks on our WhatsApp, telephone and free-assessment links, and the questions chosen in our help chat, together with the page on which they occurred; these counts are anonymous too.</li>
        <li><strong>Enquiry source</strong> &mdash; while you browse, your browser keeps a short note in <code>sessionStorage</code>, which is cleared when you close the tab. The note records the first page you opened on our website and the website that sent you (if any). It also records any advertising tags in the link you followed (for example <code>utm_source</code>, or a Google or Facebook click ID). If you send us an enquiry or request a guide, this note is sent with the form, so that we know which page or advertisement led to it. It is not shared with anyone else.</li>
        {clarityEnabled && (
          <li><strong>Microsoft Clarity</strong> &mdash; we use Clarity for anonymised heatmaps and session recordings to understand how visitors use the site and improve it. Clarity sets first-party cookies and, by default, masks sensitive content (text input is recorded as asterisks). Microsoft processes the data on our behalf and does not use it for advertising. Clarity loads on every visit; if you prefer not to be recorded, you can block scripts from <code>clarity.ms</code> with a content-blocking extension or your browser&rsquo;s tracking protection, and the website works fully without it. See <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/en-us/privacystatement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Microsoft&rsquo;s Privacy Statement</a>.</li>
        )}
      </ul>
      <p>We do not use Google Analytics, Facebook Pixel, or other third-party advertising trackers.</p>

      <h2>3. How we use your data</h2>
      <p>We use the information you provide only to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Respond to your enquiry or programme question</li>
        <li>Send you the free resource or guide you requested</li>
        <li>Understand which pages and advertisements lead to enquiries, so that we can improve them</li>
        <li>Provide updates about our programmes, if you have opted in</li>
        <li>Improve our website and services based on aggregate usage data</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not sell, rent, or share your personal data with third parties for marketing purposes.</p>

      <h2>4. Data retention</h2>
      <p>We keep your personal data only as long as we need it for the purpose it was collected for, or as long as the law requires. We typically keep enquiry records for up to 24 months. You may request deletion of your data at any time (see Section 6).</p>

      <h2>5. Data security</h2>
      <p>We take reasonable steps to protect your personal data from unauthorised access, disclosure, or loss. Our contact forms are processed through Formspree, a secure third-party form service. Email communications are transmitted over encrypted connections (TLS).</p>
      <p>No way of sending data over the internet is entirely secure. We work hard to protect your data, but we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>

      <h2>6. Your rights under the PDPA</h2>
      <p>Under Singapore&rsquo;s Personal Data Protection Act, you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Access</strong> &mdash; request a copy of the personal data we hold about you</li>
        <li><strong>Correction</strong> &mdash; request that we correct any inaccurate or incomplete data</li>
        <li><strong>Withdrawal of consent</strong> &mdash; withdraw consent to our use of your data at any time (this does not affect the lawfulness of prior processing)</li>
        <li><strong>Erasure</strong> &mdash; request deletion of your personal data, subject to any legal retention obligations</li>
      </ul>
      <p>To exercise any of these rights, contact our Data Protection Officer at <a href="mailto:jeremy@a-worthy.com">jeremy@a-worthy.com</a>. We will respond within 30 days.</p>

      <h2>7. Third-party services</h2>
      <p>Our website works with the following third-party services, each governed by its own privacy policy:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Formspree</strong> &mdash; contact form processing (<a href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy</a>)</li>
        <li><strong>WhatsApp (Meta)</strong> &mdash; messaging (<a href="https://www.whatsapp.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">whatsapp.com/legal/privacy-policy</a>)</li>
        <li><strong>Plausible Analytics</strong> &mdash; cookieless analytics (<a href="https://plausible.io/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">plausible.io/privacy</a>)</li>
        {clarityEnabled && (
          <li><strong>Microsoft Clarity</strong> &mdash; heatmaps and session-recording analytics (<a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/en-us/privacystatement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy.microsoft.com</a>)</li>
        )}
        <li><strong>The A-Worthy Whiteboard</strong> &mdash; online tuition sessions are conducted on our own learning platform. Lesson audio, video, and whiteboard content (including session recordings made available to enrolled students) are processed by A-Worthy in accordance with this policy.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>8. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The &ldquo;Last updated&rdquo; date at the top of this page reflects the most recent revision. If you continue to use our website after we post changes, you accept the updated policy.</p>

      <h2>9. Contact us</h2>
      <p>For any privacy-related questions or to exercise your PDPA rights, please contact:</p>
      <address>
        <strong>A-Worthy Pte Ltd</strong><br />
        Data Protection Officer<br />
        Email: <a href="mailto:jeremy@a-worthy.com">jeremy@a-worthy.com</a><br />
        Phone: <a href="tel:+6589913181">+65 8991 3181</a><br />
        Online tuition &mdash; Singapore-wide
      </address>

      <p class="policy-links">See also: <a href="/accessibility/">Accessibility statement</a> &middot; <a href="/contact/">Contact us</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* 45rem = 720px up to 1440px; in rem so the measure grows with the root
     size at >=1441px (a px cap left ~55-character lines and a 3-line h1 on
     1920/2560 screens once the type had scaled up) */
  .policy-content {
    max-width: 45rem;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }
  .policy-title {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    font-weight: 900;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  /* Keep the em dash on line 1 and never split "A-Worthy" at its hyphen */
  .policy-title .nowrap {
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  /* Don't break the domain link at its own hyphen ("a-" / "worthy.com") */
  .policy-content a[href^="https://a-worthy.com"] {
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .policy-updated {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  .policy-content h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 2rem 0 1rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }
  .policy-content ul {
    margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem 1.5rem;
  }
  .policy-content li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .policy-content a {
    color: var(--color-accent-text);
  }
  /* Contact block — an ink-bordered well, like the LMS read-only panels */
  .policy-content address {
    font-style: normal;
    background: var(--bg-muted);
    border: 2px solid var(--color-ink);
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem;
    line-height: 1.9;
  }
  /* <address> sits outside the global p/li/dd/td underline rule — links in
     the well must not rely on colour alone, and get the coarse-pointer
     tap padding the global rule gives running-text links */
  .policy-content address a {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 0.15em;
  }
  /* Touch: each contact line becomes a 40px row and the email / phone links
     fill it (they were 31px targets), without the padded boxes overlapping */
  @media (pointer: coarse) {
    .policy-content address {
      line-height: 2.4;
    }
    .policy-content address a {
      padding-block: 0.55rem;
    }
  }
  .policy-content code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85em;
    font-weight: 700;
    background: var(--bg-muted);
    border: 1.5px solid var(--ink-faint);
    padding: 0.1em 0.4em;
    border-radius: 6px;
  }
  .policy-links {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 2px dashed var(--ink-faint);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
</style>
